# Astro Bot (PPSA21564): flip-anchored route to the WORLD MAP under headless boot_trace.
#
# reach-first-level.pad is calibrated for a frontend that flips far more slowly per wall-second than
# headless boot_trace does: its wall-time pulses are all spent by 96 s while the run is only near
# frame 1100, so its f3800+ anchors are never reached and the guest stalls at title_controller_ship.
# This route uses the f730-960 pacing the retained world-map captures were produced with, and stops
# at the world map rather than continuing into a level.
#
# Verify against PROSPER_PAD_SCRIPT_LOG=1 and the observed flip counter before reusing on another
# frontend — pacing, not button order, is what makes a route frontend-specific.
f730-760:cross
f780-810:cross
f830-860:options
f880-910:cross
f930-960:cross
f980-1010:options
f1030-1060:cross
f1080-1110:cross
f1130-1160:options
f1180-1210:cross
